1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,623
What's today's video about? Help! SOS in Japanese!

2
00:00:09,218 --> 00:00:15,900
At some point in the video, a question will appear in Japanese. If you catch it, leave a comment!

3
00:00:17,808 --> 00:00:19,680
Scene 1: Lost and Found / Handling Lost Items

4
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:22,014
Excuse me.

5
00:00:22,038 --> 00:00:24,571
Yes, how can I help you?

6
00:00:24,594 --> 00:00:30,565
I left my bag on the train.

7
00:00:30,589 --> 00:00:33,922
Oh, your bag?

8
00:00:33,945 --> 00:00:36,778
That’s terrible!

9
00:00:36,801 --> 00:00:41,135
Yes, I’m really in trouble.

10
00:00:41,158 --> 00:00:44,235
Which train did you take?

11
00:00:44,258 --> 00:00:47,091
Which train?

12
00:00:47,114 --> 00:00:51,281
Sorry, I’m not sure.

13
00:00:51,304 --> 00:00:54,304
It was a green train.

14
00:00:54,327 --> 00:00:57,805
A green train, got it.

15
00:00:57,828 --> 00:01:00,116
Was it the Yamanote Line?

16
00:01:00,140 --> 00:01:02,873
Yamanote Line?

17
00:01:02,896 --> 00:01:07,107
Sorry, I don’t understand.

18
00:01:07,130 --> 00:01:11,164
It’s the circular line in Tokyo.

19
00:01:11,187 --> 00:01:13,641
Ah, yes!

20
00:01:13,664 --> 00:01:16,464
The circular train.

21
00:01:16,487 --> 00:01:19,891
What time did the train depart?

22
00:01:19,915 --> 00:01:25,115
I arrived here at 12:10.

23
00:01:25,138 --> 00:01:27,905
12:10, okay.

24
00:01:27,928 --> 00:01:30,694
Which car were you in?

25
00:01:30,717 --> 00:01:33,984
Which car?

26
00:01:34,007 --> 00:01:37,774
Sorry, I don’t know.

27
00:01:37,797 --> 00:01:41,063
Was it the front of the train?

28
00:01:41,086 --> 00:01:43,383
Or the middle?

29
00:01:43,407 --> 00:01:47,247
Ah, the front!

30
00:01:47,271 --> 00:01:50,271
I boarded through the front door.

31
00:01:50,294 --> 00:01:53,861
Where did you place your bag?

32
00:01:53,884 --> 00:01:56,089
The overhead rack...

33
00:01:56,113 --> 00:01:59,313
I put it on the overhead rack.

34
00:01:59,336 --> 00:02:01,669
What does the bag look like?

35
00:02:01,692 --> 00:02:05,225
It’s a black backpack.

36
00:02:05,248 --> 00:02:08,982
How big is it?

37
00:02:09,005 --> 00:02:11,771
About this big.

38
00:02:11,794 --> 00:02:14,628
It’s not very large.

39
00:02:14,651 --> 00:02:18,229
Does it have any markings?

40
00:02:18,253 --> 00:02:24,106
Markings... oh, there’s a white star.

41
00:02:24,129 --> 00:02:27,562
What’s inside?

42
00:02:27,585 --> 00:02:32,224
My passport and wallet.

43
00:02:32,248 --> 00:02:35,381
Losing your passport is a big concern.

44
00:02:35,404 --> 00:02:39,004
Yes, I don’t have it.

45
00:02:39,027 --> 00:02:42,960
Without my passport, I’m really in trouble.

46
00:02:42,983 --> 00:02:44,784
Understood.

47
00:02:44,807 --> 00:02:49,048
I’ll contact the next station now.

48
00:02:49,072 --> 00:02:51,239
Thank you so much.

49
00:02:51,262 --> 00:02:54,329
Please take a seat and wait.

50
00:02:54,352 --> 00:02:58,118
Okay, I’ll wait here.

51
00:02:58,141 --> 00:03:02,475
Could I have your name and phone number, please?

52
00:03:02,499 --> 00:03:05,111
I'm Maria.

53
00:03:05,134 --> 00:03:14,610
My phone number is 090-1234-5678.

54
00:03:14,634 --> 00:03:16,573
Maria, right?

55
00:03:16,596 --> 00:03:20,196
I'll look into it, so please don't worry.

56
00:03:20,219 --> 00:03:22,794
Thank you so much.

57
00:03:22,817 --> 00:03:29,922
Check the description and top comment for a link to review today's video! *Note: The site may be removed without prior notice.

58
00:03:29,922 --> 00:03:31,422
Scene 2: Asking for Directions & Charging Your Phone

59
00:03:31,422 --> 00:03:33,692
Excuse me...

60
00:03:33,715 --> 00:03:36,515
Yes, how can I help?

61
00:03:36,538 --> 00:03:40,072
I'm... lost.

62
00:03:40,095 --> 00:03:42,786
Where are you trying to go?

63
00:03:42,809 --> 00:03:46,142
I need to get to Sakura Hospital.

64
00:03:46,165 --> 00:03:48,899
Sakura Hospital, got it.

65
00:03:48,922 --> 00:03:53,055
Is it far from here?

66
00:03:53,078 --> 00:03:57,173
No, it's not too far.

67
00:03:57,197 --> 00:04:02,364
I wanted to look it up on my phone, but it's not working.

68
00:04:02,387 --> 00:04:04,682
What happened?

69
00:04:04,705 --> 00:04:06,579
Juuden...?

70
00:04:06,603 --> 00:04:09,173
It's out of battery.

71
00:04:09,196 --> 00:04:11,997
The screen is completely black.

72
00:04:12,021 --> 00:04:16,699
Ah, it ran out of charge.

73
00:04:16,722 --> 00:04:19,656
That's a problem.

74
00:04:19,679 --> 00:04:24,246
Yeah, I have no idea where I am.

75
00:04:24,269 --> 00:04:28,002
Go straight from here.

76
00:04:28,025 --> 00:04:30,225
Straight, okay.

77
00:04:30,248 --> 00:04:35,668
Turn right at the first traffic light.

78
00:04:35,691 --> 00:04:37,625
Shingou...?

79
00:04:37,648 --> 00:04:41,648
Sorry, what's a 'shingou'?

80
00:04:41,671 --> 00:04:44,755
It's the red and green lights.

81
00:04:44,778 --> 00:04:47,745
Where cars stop.

82
00:04:47,769 --> 00:04:50,202
Oh, I see!

83
00:04:50,225 --> 00:04:53,958
First light, then right?

84
00:04:53,981 --> 00:04:55,982
That's right.

85
00:04:56,005 --> 00:04:59,488
After turning right, you'll see a bank.

86
00:04:59,512 --> 00:05:01,312
Ginkou?

87
00:05:01,335 --> 00:05:04,135
A place for money?

88
00:05:04,158 --> 00:05:06,891
Yes, exactly.

89
00:05:06,914 --> 00:05:12,126
Next to the bank, there's a big white building.

90
00:05:12,150 --> 00:05:15,883
Next to the bank, a white building?

91
00:05:15,906 --> 00:05:20,981
Yes, the first floor of that building is Sakura Hospital.

92
00:05:21,005 --> 00:05:23,571
First floor...

93
00:05:23,594 --> 00:05:25,528
Understood.

94
00:05:25,551 --> 00:05:28,166
How long does it take to walk?

95
00:05:28,189 --> 00:05:31,122
About 5 minutes.

96
00:05:31,145 --> 00:05:33,158
Five minutes, okay.

97
00:05:33,182 --> 00:05:38,042
Be careful—it's raining right now.

98
00:05:38,065 --> 00:05:39,799
Thank you so much.

99
00:05:39,822 --> 00:05:45,555
There's also a big green sign in front of the hospital.

100
00:05:45,578 --> 00:05:47,145
Kanban?

101
00:05:47,168 --> 00:05:51,171
Sorry, I don't know what a 'kanban' is.

102
00:05:51,194 --> 00:05:56,027
It's a big board or paper with writing on it.

103
00:05:56,050 --> 00:05:59,089
Oh, you need my autograph?

104
00:05:59,113 --> 00:06:01,080
Understood.

105
00:06:01,103 --> 00:06:02,948
I'll be right there.

106
00:06:02,971 --> 00:06:05,505
Please take care on your way.

107
00:06:05,528 --> 00:06:09,306
Thank you so much, really.

108
00:06:09,329 --> 00:06:14,646
If you caught that, leave a comment!

109
00:06:14,646 --> 00:06:16,146
Scene 3: How to Find Your Lost Friend

110
00:06:16,146 --> 00:06:19,079
Excuse me...

111
00:06:19,102 --> 00:06:21,969
Yes, how can I help you?

112
00:06:21,992 --> 00:06:24,525
I can't find my friend.

113
00:06:24,548 --> 00:06:27,402
Where did you get separated?

114
00:06:27,426 --> 00:06:29,904
Separated...?

115
00:06:29,927 --> 00:06:34,171
Sorry, I don’t understand.

116
00:06:34,194 --> 00:06:38,283
Where did you and your friend part ways?

117
00:06:38,306 --> 00:06:41,873
In front of that shop over there.

118
00:06:41,896 --> 00:06:44,929
What does your friend look like?

119
00:06:44,952 --> 00:06:48,596
He’s a tall guy.

120
00:06:48,620 --> 00:06:51,226
What color is his shirt?

121
00:06:51,249 --> 00:06:54,730
He’s wearing a blue shirt.

122
00:06:54,754 --> 00:06:57,200
What about his pants?

123
00:06:57,223 --> 00:07:00,361
He’s wearing black pants.

124
00:07:00,385 --> 00:07:03,419
What’s your friend’s name?

125
00:07:03,442 --> 00:07:05,808
John.

126
00:07:05,831 --> 00:07:09,465
Does John speak Japanese?

127
00:07:09,488 --> 00:07:12,862
No, not at all.

128
00:07:12,885 --> 00:07:15,764
That’s concerning.

129
00:07:15,787 --> 00:07:20,191
Yeah, and I can’t reach him on his phone either.

130
00:07:20,214 --> 00:07:24,081
Is John wearing a hat?

131
00:07:24,104 --> 00:07:28,104
Yes, a white one.

132
00:07:28,127 --> 00:07:30,777
Is he carrying a bag?

133
00:07:30,801 --> 00:07:33,834
He has a brown bag.

134
00:07:33,857 --> 00:07:37,794
Alright, let’s make an announcement over the PA system.

135
00:07:37,818 --> 00:07:40,351
A PA announcement...?

136
00:07:40,374 --> 00:07:45,174
We’ll call out John’s name over the speakers.

137
00:07:45,197 --> 00:07:47,485
Oh, please do.

138
00:07:47,509 --> 00:07:50,924
Please write his name here.

139
00:07:50,947 --> 00:07:53,780
Okay, I’ve written it.

140
00:07:53,803 --> 00:07:57,537
Please wait here until we’re done.

141
00:07:57,560 --> 00:07:59,893
Thank you so much.

142
00:07:59,916 --> 00:08:01,416
Scene 4: Trouble at Payment

143
00:08:01,416 --> 00:08:03,069
Excuse me.

144
00:08:03,093 --> 00:08:05,662
Check, please.

145
00:08:05,685 --> 00:08:07,088
Sure.

146
00:08:07,112 --> 00:08:10,752
Your total is 2,500 yen.

147
00:08:10,775 --> 00:08:12,020
Sure.

148
00:08:12,044 --> 00:08:14,054
One moment, please.

149
00:08:14,078 --> 00:08:15,487
Sure.

150
00:08:15,510 --> 00:08:16,809
Huh...

151
00:08:16,832 --> 00:08:19,273
I don’t have my wallet.

152
00:08:19,296 --> 00:08:22,663
Isn’t it in your bag?

153
00:08:22,686 --> 00:08:26,486
In my bag... No, it’s not.

154
00:08:26,509 --> 00:08:28,563
What should I do?

155
00:08:28,586 --> 00:08:31,520
Do you have a credit card?

156
00:08:31,543 --> 00:08:35,509
My cards are in my wallet too.

157
00:08:35,532 --> 00:08:39,104
Can you pay with your phone?

158
00:08:39,128 --> 00:08:43,304
I don’t have any money on my phone.

159
00:08:43,327 --> 00:08:45,766
This is awkward.

160
00:08:45,790 --> 00:08:48,361
I'm really sorry about this,

161
00:08:48,384 --> 00:08:50,617
I don't have any money on me.

162
00:08:50,640 --> 00:08:54,440
Did you come here with someone today?

163
00:08:54,463 --> 00:08:57,230
No, I'm alone.

164
00:08:57,253 --> 00:09:00,686
Do you have any friends living nearby?

165
00:09:00,709 --> 00:09:02,109
Yes,

166
00:09:02,132 --> 00:09:05,699
I have a friend who works at a company nearby.

167
00:09:05,722 --> 00:09:09,759
Could you give them a call?

168
00:09:09,782 --> 00:09:11,216
Yes,

169
00:09:11,239 --> 00:09:13,306
I'll call them.

170
00:09:13,329 --> 00:09:15,262
Alright,

171
00:09:15,285 --> 00:09:17,218
go ahead and try.

172
00:09:17,241 --> 00:09:21,679
Hello, Ken? Please help me out.

173
00:09:21,703 --> 00:09:25,389
Could you bring some money to the shop?

174
00:09:25,412 --> 00:09:28,145
Does it look like your friend can come?

175
00:09:28,168 --> 00:09:29,643
Sure.

176
00:09:29,667 --> 00:09:33,037
He's on his way now.

177
00:09:33,060 --> 00:09:34,798
That's a relief.

178
00:09:34,822 --> 00:09:37,555
Okay, please wait here.

179
00:09:37,578 --> 00:09:40,270
I'm really sorry about this.

180
00:09:40,293 --> 00:09:41,793
Scene 5: Handling Key Lockouts in a Room

181
00:09:41,793 --> 00:09:44,626
Excuse me,

182
00:09:44,649 --> 00:09:46,783
is this the front desk?

183
00:09:46,807 --> 00:09:49,773
Yes, this is the front desk.

184
00:09:49,796 --> 00:09:51,763
What happened?

185
00:09:51,786 --> 00:09:56,121
I left my room key inside.

186
00:09:56,144 --> 00:10:00,883
You left the key inside and closed the door?

187
00:10:00,907 --> 00:10:04,440
Yes, the door closed.

188
00:10:04,463 --> 00:10:06,663
And now it won't open.

189
00:10:06,686 --> 00:10:08,853
Ah, you're locked out.

190
00:10:08,876 --> 00:10:10,649
Understood.

191
00:10:10,672 --> 00:10:12,885
Locked out...?

192
00:10:12,909 --> 00:10:15,581
Sorry,

193
00:10:15,604 --> 00:10:18,051
I don't understand the term.

194
00:10:18,074 --> 00:10:20,307
No problem,

195
00:10:20,330 --> 00:10:22,599
this happens quite often.

196
00:10:22,623 --> 00:10:25,870
I'm in the hallway right now.

197
00:10:25,894 --> 00:10:28,627
What's your room number?

198
00:10:28,650 --> 00:10:31,850
Room 305.

199
00:10:31,873 --> 00:10:35,529
Maria in Room 305, correct?

200
00:10:35,553 --> 00:10:38,197
Yes, exactly.

201
00:10:38,221 --> 00:10:40,503
I'll be right there.

202
00:10:40,526 --> 00:10:42,224
Thank you,

203
00:10:42,247 --> 00:10:44,614
please hurry.

204
00:10:44,637 --> 00:10:47,682
I'll bring the master key.

205
00:10:47,706 --> 00:10:50,375
A master key?

206
00:10:50,398 --> 00:10:52,970
It's a special key

207
00:10:52,993 --> 00:10:55,207
that can open the door.

208
00:10:55,231 --> 00:10:58,397
Oh, I see!

209
00:10:58,420 --> 00:11:01,393
Isn't the hallway a bit chilly?

210
00:11:01,417 --> 00:11:05,019
Yes, it's a little cold.

211
00:11:05,042 --> 00:11:08,414
I'll be there soon, so please wait.

212
00:11:08,438 --> 00:11:12,271
Okay, I'll wait by the door.

213
00:11:12,294 --> 00:11:13,794
Scene 6: How to Respond When You're Sick

214
00:11:13,794 --> 00:11:15,728
Excuse me.

215
00:11:15,751 --> 00:11:19,122
I have a terrible stomachache.

216
00:11:19,145 --> 00:11:21,379
Are you okay?

217
00:11:21,402 --> 00:11:24,402
You don’t look well.

218
00:11:24,424 --> 00:11:27,916
It’s been hurting since this morning.

219
00:11:27,940 --> 00:11:30,575
Do you have a fever?

220
00:11:30,598 --> 00:11:35,469
I checked earlier, and it was 38°C (100.4°F).

221
00:11:35,492 --> 00:11:38,026
That’s not good.

222
00:11:38,049 --> 00:11:40,382
Let’s go to the hospital.

223
00:11:40,405 --> 00:11:44,383
Is there a big hospital nearby?

224
00:11:44,406 --> 00:11:46,022
Sure.

225
00:11:46,046 --> 00:11:48,700
There’s one near the station.

226
00:11:48,723 --> 00:11:52,557
Can we walk there?

227
00:11:52,579 --> 00:11:55,979
No, walking isn’t an option.

228
00:11:56,002 --> 00:11:58,697
I’ll call a taxi.

229
00:11:58,721 --> 00:12:00,409
Please do.

230
00:12:00,432 --> 00:12:03,249
It really hurts.

231
00:12:03,273 --> 00:12:06,039
Are you feeling nauseous?

232
00:12:06,062 --> 00:12:11,029
Nauseous? Sorry, I don’t understand.

233
00:12:11,052 --> 00:12:15,385
Do you feel like throwing up?

234
00:12:15,408 --> 00:12:19,342
No, I’m okay on that.

235
00:12:19,365 --> 00:12:22,839
But I feel dizzy.

236
00:12:22,862 --> 00:12:24,904
Understood.

237
00:12:24,927 --> 00:12:27,346
Please sit here.

238
00:12:27,369 --> 00:12:29,003
Thank you so much.

239
00:12:29,026 --> 00:12:33,459
Do you have your insurance card or passport?

240
00:12:33,482 --> 00:12:35,449
Insurance card?

241
00:12:35,472 --> 00:12:40,157
It’s an important card you use at the hospital.

242
00:12:40,180 --> 00:12:43,347
Oh, I don’t have the card.

243
00:12:43,370 --> 00:12:46,536
But my passport is in my bag.

244
00:12:46,559 --> 00:12:48,893
That’s good.

245
00:12:48,916 --> 00:12:51,116
The taxi’s here.

246
00:12:51,138 --> 00:12:53,172
Thank you so much.

247
00:12:53,195 --> 00:12:54,695
Scene 7: Coping with Sudden Rain / Finding Shelter from the Downpour

248
00:12:54,695 --> 00:12:59,495
Whoa, it suddenly started raining!

249
00:12:59,518 --> 00:13:03,518
It really did—pouring down!

250
00:13:03,541 --> 00:13:07,107
I don’t have an umbrella.

251
00:13:07,130 --> 00:13:11,330
Neither do I. What should we do?

252
00:13:11,353 --> 00:13:15,753
Let’s take shelter here for now.

253
00:13:15,776 --> 00:13:18,143
Good idea.

254
00:13:18,166 --> 00:13:21,933
But it doesn’t look like it’s stopping anytime soon.

255
00:13:21,956 --> 00:13:25,289
How far is the station from here?

256
00:13:25,312 --> 00:13:29,316
About a 15-minute walk.

257
00:13:29,339 --> 00:13:32,630
15 minutes is too far.

258
00:13:32,654 --> 00:13:34,220
We’ll get soaked.

259
00:13:34,243 --> 00:13:37,677
There’s a convenience store nearby.

260
00:13:37,700 --> 00:13:41,433
Can we buy umbrellas there?

261
00:13:41,456 --> 00:13:45,307
Yes, they sell plastic umbrellas.

262
00:13:45,331 --> 00:13:47,664
Plastic umbrellas?

263
00:13:47,687 --> 00:13:52,221
Cheap, white plastic ones.

264
00:13:52,244 --> 00:13:54,889
Oh, I see!

265
00:13:54,912 --> 00:13:58,146
Where’s the convenience store?

266
00:13:58,169 --> 00:14:02,102
Just around that corner.

267
00:14:02,125 --> 00:14:05,170
Is it about a minute if we run?

268
00:14:05,194 --> 00:14:09,481
Yeah, it’s right there—let’s run!

269
00:14:09,504 --> 00:14:11,237
Understood.

270
00:14:11,260 --> 00:14:13,194
Ready?

271
00:14:13,217 --> 00:14:15,817
Yep, let’s go!

272
00:14:15,840 --> 00:14:17,573
Let's run!

273
00:14:17,596 --> 00:14:19,683
Let's hurry!

274
00:14:19,706 --> 00:14:21,206
Scene 8: Confirming Lost Items

275
00:14:21,206 --> 00:14:23,102
Excuse me.

276
00:14:23,126 --> 00:14:26,782
Was it the taxi driver from earlier?

277
00:14:26,805 --> 00:14:30,609
Yes, that's me. What happened?

278
00:14:30,633 --> 00:14:34,600
I might have dropped my passport.

279
00:14:34,623 --> 00:14:37,463
Was it in the taxi?

280
00:14:37,486 --> 00:14:41,536
I think it's either on the seat or the floor.

281
00:14:41,560 --> 00:14:43,595
Understood.

282
00:14:43,619 --> 00:14:47,055
I'll check the back seat.

283
00:14:47,078 --> 00:14:48,777
Please do.

284
00:14:48,800 --> 00:14:51,267
I'm really in trouble here.

285
00:14:51,290 --> 00:14:55,265
Oh, there's something under the seat.

286
00:14:55,288 --> 00:14:57,255
Really?

287
00:14:57,278 --> 00:14:59,094
Let me see.

288
00:14:59,118 --> 00:15:01,151
Is this it?

289
00:15:01,174 --> 00:15:03,974
It looks like a red notebook.

290
00:15:03,997 --> 00:15:08,442
No, that's not my notebook.

291
00:15:08,465 --> 00:15:12,322
Then, let me check the door pocket.

292
00:15:12,346 --> 00:15:14,397
Did you find it?

293
00:15:14,420 --> 00:15:18,063
No, it's not here.

294
00:15:18,087 --> 00:15:20,053
What should I do?

295
00:15:20,076 --> 00:15:23,760
I can't board the plane without my passport.

296
00:15:23,783 --> 00:15:28,017
Please check your bag again.

297
00:15:28,040 --> 00:15:31,378
I already checked my bag earlier.

298
00:15:31,402 --> 00:15:34,640
How about the small pockets?

299
00:15:34,663 --> 00:15:37,152
Pockets?

300
00:15:37,176 --> 00:15:39,409
Oh, here it is!

301
00:15:39,432 --> 00:15:41,565
Found it!

302
00:15:41,588 --> 00:15:43,388
That’s good.

303
00:15:43,411 --> 00:15:45,978
I'm so relieved it's found.

304
00:15:46,001 --> 00:15:49,134
I'm really sorry about that.

305
00:15:49,157 --> 00:15:50,657
Scene 9: How to Handle a Toilet Water Leak

306
00:15:50,657 --> 00:15:54,191
Hello, is this the management company?

307
00:15:54,214 --> 00:15:56,816
Yes, exactly.

308
00:15:56,839 --> 00:15:58,613
Yes, how can I help you?

309
00:15:58,636 --> 00:16:02,203
The toilet won't stop running.

310
00:16:02,226 --> 00:16:05,294
Is the water continuously flowing?

311
00:16:05,317 --> 00:16:09,084
Yes, it's pouring out.

312
00:16:09,107 --> 00:16:11,707
Is the floor wet?

313
00:16:11,730 --> 00:16:15,863
Yes, the floor is flooded.

314
00:16:15,886 --> 00:16:17,553
Understood.

315
00:16:17,576 --> 00:16:21,109
First, turn off the main valve.

316
00:16:21,132 --> 00:16:23,699
The main valve...?

317
00:16:23,722 --> 00:16:27,522
Sorry, I don’t know.

318
00:16:27,545 --> 00:16:32,345
It's a small handle to stop the water.

319
00:16:32,368 --> 00:16:34,934
It's located under the toilet tank.

320
00:16:34,957 --> 00:16:37,557
Under the tank...

321
00:16:37,580 --> 00:16:40,514
Oh, is this it?

322
00:16:40,537 --> 00:16:44,070
But it's too tight to turn.

323
00:16:44,093 --> 00:16:46,696
Do you have any tools?

324
00:16:46,720 --> 00:16:48,795
Tools?

325
00:16:48,818 --> 00:16:53,384
Sorry, I don’t understand.

326
00:16:53,407 --> 00:16:57,343
Like a screwdriver or a wrench.

327
00:16:57,367 --> 00:17:00,824
No, I don't have any tools.

328
00:17:00,848 --> 00:17:02,814
Understood.

329
00:17:02,837 --> 00:17:06,087
A repair person will be there shortly.

330
00:17:06,111 --> 00:17:08,524
How soon will they arrive?

331
00:17:08,548 --> 00:17:12,036
We can get there in about thirty minutes.

332
00:17:12,059 --> 00:17:14,912
Please come as soon as possible.

333
00:17:14,935 --> 00:17:17,701
Water is leaking into the room.

334
00:17:17,724 --> 00:17:19,891
I'll rush over right away.

335
00:17:19,914 --> 00:17:22,482
Please wipe the water with a towel.

336
00:17:22,506 --> 00:17:24,577
Understood.

337
00:17:24,600 --> 00:17:26,979
I'll use a towel.

338
00:17:27,003 --> 00:17:30,736
I'll be right there, so please wait.

339
00:17:30,759 --> 00:17:33,126
Thank you so much.

340
00:17:33,149 --> 00:17:34,649
Scene 10: Earthquake Response / How to Stay Safe During an Earthquake

341
00:17:34,649 --> 00:17:37,582
Ah! It's an earthquake!

342
00:17:37,605 --> 00:17:39,699
It's shaking!

343
00:17:39,723 --> 00:17:41,856
Stay calm.

344
00:17:41,879 --> 00:17:45,049
Get under the desk.

345
00:17:45,073 --> 00:17:48,212
I'm scared. What should I do?

346
00:17:48,235 --> 00:17:50,082
It's going to be okay.

347
00:17:50,106 --> 00:17:52,873
Protect your head.

348
00:17:52,896 --> 00:17:56,181
The shaking is really strong!

349
00:17:56,204 --> 00:18:00,541
It'll stop soon, so don't move.

350
00:18:00,565 --> 00:18:02,898
It'll stop...?

351
00:18:02,921 --> 00:18:07,321
It means the shaking will end.

352
00:18:07,344 --> 00:18:10,615
Oh, the shaking stopped.

353
00:18:10,639 --> 00:18:13,135
That’s good.

354
00:18:13,159 --> 00:18:15,425
Are you hurt?

355
00:18:15,448 --> 00:18:18,248
Yes, I'm fine.

356
00:18:18,271 --> 00:18:20,838
But I'm still scared.

357
00:18:20,861 --> 00:18:23,828
Where should we go next?

358
00:18:23,851 --> 00:18:26,984
Should we go outside?

359
00:18:27,007 --> 00:18:31,740
No, it's dangerous outside—glass might fall.

360
00:18:31,763 --> 00:18:34,763
So, should we stay here?

361
00:18:34,786 --> 00:18:39,120
Let's turn on the TV and check the news.

362
00:18:39,142 --> 00:18:40,909
The news?

363
00:18:40,932 --> 00:18:43,509
I mean the earthquake updates.

364
00:18:43,533 --> 00:18:46,171
We should watch the news for updates.

365
00:18:46,194 --> 00:18:48,527
Understood.

366
00:18:48,550 --> 00:18:50,750
Is a tsunami coming?

367
00:18:50,773 --> 00:18:55,632
We're far from the sea, so we'll be fine.

368
00:18:55,655 --> 00:18:57,990
Should we go to an evacuation center?

369
00:18:58,014 --> 00:18:59,947
An evacuation center?

370
00:18:59,970 --> 00:19:03,170
It's a safe place, like a shelter.

371
00:19:03,193 --> 00:19:05,360
We can go to the elementary school.

372
00:19:05,383 --> 00:19:08,149
Will you come with me?

373
00:19:08,172 --> 00:19:11,572
Yes, let's go together.

374
00:19:11,595 --> 00:19:13,873
Please bring your belongings.

375
00:19:13,897 --> 00:19:15,744
Understood.

376
00:19:15,767 --> 00:19:18,101
Thank you so much.